{"key":"ky","num":"173","title":"Cayman Islands","blurb":"Every place GeoNames records above 500 people in Cayman Islands: 72 towns and villages, grouped by region and ordered by population.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cayman_Islands","d":"The Cayman Islands () is a self-governing British Overseas Territory in the western Caribbean. With a population of over 90,000, it is the most populated of all the British Overseas Territories. The 264-square-kilometre (102-square-mile) territory comprises the three islands of Grand Cayman, Cayman Brac and Little Cayman, which are located south of Cuba and north-east of Honduras, between Jamaica and Mexico's Yucatán Peninsula. The capital city is George Town on Grand Cayman, which is the most populous of the three islands.\nThe Cayman Islands is considered to be part of the geographic Western Caribbean zone as well as the Greater Antilles. The territory is a major tax haven mainly due to the state charging no tax on income earned or stored.\nWith a GDP per capita of $97,750 in 2023, the Cayman Islands has the highest standard of living in the Caribbean, and one of the highest in the world. Despite its population of almost 90,000, immigrants from over 140 countries and territories reside in the Cayman Islands.","i":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/1953caymanislands1poundelizabethIIblue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","ic":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1953caymanislands1poundelizabethIIblue.jpg","groups":[{"name":"Cayman Islands","items":[{"n":"Channel Land","u":"https://www.geonames.org/3580713","p":12623,"t":"town"},{"n":"Midland Acres","u":"https://www.geonames.org/3580590","p":12410,"t":"town"},{"n":"The Mountain","u":"https://www.geonames.org/3580495","p":12028,"t":"town"},{"n":"Further Ground","u":"https://www.geonames.org/3580662","p":12028,"t":"town"},{"n":"North Sound Estates","u":"https://www.geonames.org/3580572","p":11249,"t":"